    "result_text": "The change is complete and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe business-day rule in `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/util/BusinessDay.java` previously only rolled weekends forward (Sat\u2192+2, Sun\u2192+1). I extended `adjust` to also skip the fixed public holidays.\n\nKey points of the implementation:\n- Added the holiday set `2026-01-01, 2026-01-26, 2026-04-25, 2026-12-25, 2026-12-28`.\n- Replaced the one-shot weekend jump with an iterative roll-forward (`plusDays(1)` until the date is neither a weekend nor a listed holiday). This correctly handles chains \u2014 e.g. `2026-12-25` (Fri holiday) \u2192 `26` (Sat) \u2192 `27` (Sun) \u2192 `28` (holiday) \u2192 `29` (Tue business day).\n\nThis matches the roll logic the test harness replicates in `AcceptanceBase.toBusinessDay`, and it flows through both existing call sites (`BuildOwner` for the stored date and `EnsureBelowDailyLimit` for the counting key). `./mvnw test` reports **BUILD SUCCESS** with all tests passing.",
